= Working memory — Simple =

'''Working memory''' is the limited mental workspace you use to keep information active while doing something with it.

If you remember a phone number long enough to type it, follow several steps in a calculation, or hold the beginning of a sentence in mind while reading the end, you are using working memory.

Working memory is limited. Too much information or too many competing tasks can make performance worse.

It is related to short-term memory, but the terms are not exactly the same. Working memory especially emphasizes using and manipulating information, not only holding it briefly.

There are several scientific models of working memory. No single model is the definition of the concept.

